<title>RUSSIA: Russia to auction 11 trln rbls in bills.</title>
<headline>Russia to auction 11 trln rbls in bills.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction seven trillion roubles of 203-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 22079) and four trillion roubles of 728-day OFZ government interest-bearing bonds on April 2, the Central Bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>Full details of the T-bill issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		   22079</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date			April 2, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			     203 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   Oct 22, 1997</p>
<p>Full details of the bond issue:</p>
<p>    Series number		   24011</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    4.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Issue date			April 2, 1997</p>
<p>    Tenor			     728 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   March 31, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon amount	   37.45 pct (186,737 rbls)</p>
<p>    First coupon date	     Oct 1, 1997</p>
<p>    Second coupon date	    April 1, 1998</p>
<p>    Third coupon date	     Sept 30, 1998</p>
<p>    Fourth coupon date	    March 31, 1999</p>
<p>The coupon rate calculated after April 1, 1997, is calculated on the results of trading in T-bills issued after January 21, 1997.</p>
<p>On April 2, the Finance Ministry will repay about 6.92 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of six-month T-bills (series 23047).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
